# held/civil/staff_runl: the staff (art weapon 4) carried in the run facing left, in the near (left) hand: the run
# changes hands with the facing as the side views always show the near one (PROPS, P2b fix B10-CIVIL-STAFF-RUN-ATLAS;
# staff_run.pxm the same facing right, where the notes are).
# PROTO6 i3 (2026-10-22; the run's lean 4 and the wider arm pump): pB carries the staff upright at the hand (no lean back), pF
# grips it 3 rows higher up the shaft (the woman's 3), pM stands it behind the head (layer neck: it no longer crosses the face),
# pK upright: the robed scholars' RUN atlases stay in B10's 64 KB.
use person
body man woman
role held staff
layer neck
anchor gripL
keys armL
z 40

view D key runB origin 0 0
|.

view D key N origin 0 0
|.

view D key runF origin 0 0
|.

view U key runB origin 0 0
|.

view U key N origin 0 0
|.

view U key runF origin 0 0
|.

